  "summary": "A double pipe (hairpin) heat exchanger is the simplest exchanger: one fluid flows in an inner tube, the other in the annulus between it and an outer pipe. Running the two fluids in opposite directions (counter-current) gives the best heat transfer. Hairpins are compact, easy to clean and handle high pressure.",
